# Architecture.md - Energy Dashboard

**Last Updated**: 2026-07-29
**Supersedes**: the vanilla-JS single-file architecture of 2026-02-15 (preserved at `Architecture.md.backup`)

---

## Overview

Residential energy monitoring dashboard for a Belgian solar + battery + grid setup,
embedded in a Flutter mobile app via WebView. Visualizes real-time and historical
energy data by fetching from two self-hosted FastAPI backends (P1 smart meter,
Sungrow inverter).

**Primary Goal**: Answer "where is my energy going right now?" in under 2 seconds,
and increasingly "am I about to set a new monthly capacity peak?" (Belgian
capaciteitstarief).

**Companion Project**: The Flutter host app provides device IDs and base URLs via
URL parameters and delivers Bearer tokens via the WebView postMessage bridge (or
the dashboard runs in cookie-based proxy mode — see Authentication).

### The 2026-07-29 Pivot

The frontend has been re-designed in Lovable (project "Energy Watch") and the
generated screens are adopted **as-is** as the new frontend. This replaces the
vanilla-JS/single-HTML-file architecture wholesale:

| Retired | Replaced by | Recorded in |
|---------|-------------|-------------|
| HC-001 Single-File Delivery (< 200 KB inlined HTML, no npm runtime deps, no bundler) | Vite-built static SPA with a dependency tree and per-asset budget (HC-005) | ADR-005 (2026-07-29) |
| ADR-001 Vanilla JavaScript Over Framework | React (TanStack Start) + TypeScript | ADR-005 (2026-07-29) |
| ADR-002 Chart.js via CDN | Bundled charting library, no CDN, no SRI exposure | ADR-007 (2026-07-29) |
| ADR-003 SVG for Power Flow (vanilla DOM manipulation) | Inline SVG retained, rendered by React components | ADR-008 (2026-07-29) |
| `scripts/build.js` inlining pipeline | `vite build` producing `dist/` static assets | ADR-005 (2026-07-29) |
| Chart.js + Google Fonts CDNs, CSP `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` | Self-hosted fonts, bundled charts, hashed assets, `script-src 'self'` | Build & Deployment |

Rationale for the pivot: v1 was functionally complete but under-delivered on the
interaction spec (no counting animations, no skeletons, no per-section staleness,
no battery visual, a Peak card without its threshold). The Lovable redesign
(`docs/REDESIGN_BRIEF.md`) delivers those screens on a modern component stack;
the 200 KB single-file constraint that justified vanilla JS no longer buys
anything once the artifact is served by our own nginx container.

What does **not** change: the two external APIs and their contracts, the sign
conventions, the credential rules, graceful degradation, dark-mode-only, poll
cadences, and the FE_design.md token system. Those all carry forward and are
restated in this document.

