## Design System Mapping (FE_design.md → Tailwind/shadcn)

`docs/FE_design.md` remains the authoritative token source (colors, type scale,
spacing, component anatomy, motion). Under the new stack it binds as follows:

- **CSS variables first**: every FE_design token is declared once as a CSS custom
  property in `src/styles.css` under `:root` — `--bg-base: #0A0E14`, `--solar:
  #F6B93B`, `--grid-import: #E17055`, `--grid-export: #00B894`,
  `--battery-charge`, `--battery-discharge`, `--home`, `--success`, `--warning`,
  `--danger`, `--accent`, `--border-subtle`, `--border-focus`, text and surface
  tokens per FE_design.md. Components reference tokens, never literal hex.
- **shadcn convention**: shadcn/ui components consume their own variable set
  (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--card`, `--primary`, `--ring`, …). Map them
  to FE_design values in the same stylesheet (`--background` ← `--bg-base`,
  `--card` ← `--bg-surface`, `--ring` ← `--border-focus`, etc.). One theme block
  only — no `.dark` class switching, no alternate palette (HC-004).
- **Tailwind theme**: energy colors exposed as Tailwind color names
  (`solar`, `grid-import`, …) that resolve to the CSS variables, so utilities and
  raw CSS agree. Exact mechanism follows the generated project's Tailwind version
  (v4 CSS-first `@theme` expected — TBC).
- **Typography**: JetBrains Mono and DM Sans **self-hosted** via bundled font
  packages (the Google Fonts CDN is retired with the CSP tightening). Data font
  used with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` so digits hold width while
  counters animate. Type scale and the units-smaller-than-numbers rule per
  FE_design.md.
- **Spacing**: 8 px grid (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64) — Tailwind's default
  scale already conforms; do not introduce off-grid values.
- **Motion**: number counters ~400 ms ease-out; flow dashes ~3 s loops; direction
  flip flash ~300 ms; everything collapses under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Accessibility**: WCAG AA contrast, 44×44 px touch targets, visible focus
  rings (`--border-focus`), aria-labels on chart data.

Lovable screens were generated from this same token system
(`docs/REDESIGN_BRIEF.md` §4); FE_design conformance review (CLAUDE.md §2.3
DESIGN gate) still applies to every presentation change after adoption.

