## Testing Strategy

The 265-test Jest+jsdom suite is bound to the vanilla IIFE modules and dies with
them. Replacement:

| Test type | Location | Tool | Target |
|-----------|----------|------|--------|
| Pure domain logic | `tests/energy/` | Vitest | **highest value — port aggressively**: flows, balance, capacity, format |
| API client & validation | `tests/api/` | Vitest, mocked `fetch` | contract shapes, auth-mode selection, allowlist, backoff, timeout, cache-on-failure |
| Config parsing | `tests/api/` | Vitest | URL params, scrubbing, allowlist rejection, postMessage schema |
| Data layer | `tests/data/` | Vitest, fake timers, injectable clock | cadence, visibility gating, backoff schedule, staleness |
| Components | `tests/components/` | Vitest + React Testing Library (jsdom) | states (skeleton/stale/offline), sign-driven rendering (accent flips, direction) |
| Fixtures | `tests/fixtures/` | JSON (carried over) | real API response shapes |

### What must be ported (not rewritten from scratch)

The pure-calculation tests encode hard-won domain knowledge — port their
assertions into TypeScript against `src/lib/energy/`:

1. **Sign-convention tests**: `computeFlows` with negative `power_w` (export),
   negative `battery_power_w` (discharge), `export_power_w = 0` firmware quirk —
   including the new invariant *"with P1 `power_w = -2000`, solar→grid flow is
   non-zero even though Sungrow `export_power_w` is 0"* (this pins the legacy
   defect fixed at port time — see Data Flow §3).
2. **Energy balance**: bucket summation, self-consumption / self-sufficiency
   clamping, zero-production and zero-consumption edges.
3. **Config validation**: all `config.test.js` cases, plus new allowlist cases.
4. **Formatting**: W/kW thresholds and precision.

Rules carried forward: no test touches real network or services; time-dependent
code takes an injectable clock (never `Date.now()` inline in business logic);
fixtures that drift from this document are a defect in one of the two —
escalate, don't silently pick a side. Coverage target: 80%+ on `src/lib/`.

