## Build & Deployment

### Pipeline

```
bun run build  →  dist/            # hashed JS/CSS chunks, index.html, fonts, assets
check-size     →  budget gate      # HC-005
Docker build   →  nginx:alpine + COPY dist/ /usr/share/nginx/html/
deploy.sh      →  upload + docker compose up on VPS (behind Caddy)
```

Replaces `scripts/build.js` (retired 2026-07-29 — inlining is meaningless with a
bundler). `deploy.sh` changes: upload the whole `dist/` directory instead of one
file; replace the 200 KB check with the size gate; the Dockerfile copies `dist/`
instead of `dist/dashboard.html`. Note the pre-existing mismatch between
`docker-compose.yml` (pulls `ghcr.io/wluyckx/energy-dashboard:latest`) and
`deploy.sh` (`docker compose build` on the VPS) — the Operator's
artifact-provenance rule (CLAUDE.md §2.5) requires resolving this to one path
during migration (M6).

### Artifact shape & size budget (replaces the 200 KB rule)

The artifact is a static `dist/` directory. Provisional budgets, **to be
calibrated against the first real build** and then pinned in `check-size.js`:

| Metric | Budget (gzipped) |
|--------|------------------|
| JS on the initial `/` route | ≤ 300 KB |
| Total JS (all routes, code-split) | ≤ 450 KB |
| CSS | ≤ 50 KB |
| Fonts (woff2, both families) | ≤ 200 KB |

Detail routes (`/grid`, `/capacity`) and the chart library should be code-split
behind route chunks where the framework makes it natural. The budget exists for
the same reason the 200 KB rule did — this loads over mobile data in a WebView —
but measures what actually matters now: compressed transfer size.

### nginx

`try_files $uri /index.html` (already present) is the SPA fallback for pushed
routes. Caching changes for the multi-file artifact: `index.html` stays
`no-cache`; hashed assets (`/assets/*`) get `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.
`/health` endpoint unchanged. Gzip already configured; keep `image/svg+xml` and
add `font/woff2` exclusion (woff2 is pre-compressed).

### CSP (tightened — fixes two standing weaknesses)

The current CSP allows `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` and loads Chart.js from an
unpinned CDN with no SRI. The new build emits only hashed external scripts and
self-hosts fonts, so:

```
default-src 'self';
script-src 'self';
style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
font-src 'self';
connect-src 'self' ${CSP_CONNECT_HOSTS};
img-src 'self' data:;
frame-ancestors 'self'
```

- `script-src` drops `'unsafe-inline'` and `cdn.jsdelivr.net` entirely. If the
  generated `index.html` contains a framework bootstrap inline script, prefer a
  build option that externalizes it; a CSP hash for that one script is the
  fallback — never a blanket `'unsafe-inline'`.
- `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` is retained for now: React/charting set inline
  `style` attributes. Tightening to `style-src-attr` is a post-migration audit
  item (R5).
- `${CSP_CONNECT_HOSTS}` remains the env-templated first-party API host list —
  the same list the base-URL allowlist validates against.
- Google Fonts (`fonts.googleapis.com` / `fonts.gstatic.com`) entries are removed.

### Environments

| Environment | Command / URL | Purpose |
|-------------|---------------|---------|
| Development | `bun run dev` (Vite dev server) | HMR, mock mode via `?mock=true` |
| Production | `dist/` served by nginx container behind Caddy | `https://dashboard.energy.wimluyckx.dev` |

