## Hard Constraints

HC numbering is continuous with the previous document; retired numbers are not
reused. (HC-004 previously lived only in CLAUDE.md — this document now owns it.)

### HC-001: Single-File Delivery — **RETIRED 2026-07-29**
Superseded by ADR-005/ADR-006 and HC-005. The constraint existed because there
was no server to serve multiple files; we have served the dashboard from our own
nginx container since the Docker deployment landed, so the premise is gone. The
budget discipline it enforced survives as HC-005's bundle budget.

### HC-002: Secure Credential Delivery
**Constraint**: Bearer tokens are delivered via the WebView postMessage bridge and
held in JS memory only. URL-param tokens are a dev/test fallback scrubbed
immediately via `history.replaceState`. In proxy mode (no token), auth rides on
cookies via `credentials: 'include'` and the dashboard never sees a token.
**Base URLs must pass host-allowlist validation before any request is made** —
an `https://` prefix check alone is a vulnerability in both auth modes.
**Forbidden**: hardcoded tokens; tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage/cookies;
tokens in console logs; tokens remaining in the URL bar; requests to
non-allowlisted hosts.

### HC-003: Graceful Degradation
**Constraint**: never a blank screen. Every component has defined skeleton,
stale, and offline states; last-known values are cached and shown with staleness
indicators; mock data is the fallback of last resort; `mock=true` always works
without credentials.
**Forbidden**: blank screens, raw error strings in the UI, unhandled exceptions
crashing the app (wrap routes in error boundaries), removing the mock module
from the production bundle.

### HC-004: Dark Mode Only
**Constraint**: one theme. No light mode, no toggle, no `prefers-color-scheme`
switching, no theme URL parameter, and — new-stack specific — **no `.dark`/light
dual palette in the Tailwind/shadcn theme**: the single token set is the theme.
Rationale in ADR-004.

### HC-005: Static Artifact, No Server Runtime (new)
**Constraint**: the production artifact is the static `dist/` directory served by
nginx. No Node/Bun process, SSR, server functions, or API routes in production
(ADR-006). Bundle budgets per Build & Deployment are enforced by
`scripts/check-size.js` as a release gate.
**Forbidden**: TanStack Start server functions, runtime environment variables
(config arrives via URL params/bridge only), any deploy shape that requires a JS
runtime on the VPS.

### HC-006: API Contracts Are Captured, Never Guessed (new)
**Constraint**: no code may read an API field that is not documented in this
file's API Integration section (or `docs/project_idea.md` for legacy detail).
An undocumented contract blocks the story (`api_contract_unknown`) until the
contract is captured from the live API and recorded here.
**Rationale**: the guessed P1-series fields in `p1-card.js` shipped a
NaN-rendering chart (Open Risk R1). Sungrow `export_power_w` is the standing
example of a field that exists but must never be read (Sign Convention
Reference).

### Domain rules (bind every change)

- Poll cadences exactly as specified (5 s / 60 s / 5 min); polling pauses when
  the document is hidden; failures back off.
- All API communication over HTTPS.
- Sign conventions per the Sign Convention Reference — non-waivable review gate.
- Colors referenced by token, never literal hex; typography and spacing per
  FE_design.md; energy values with correct units and precision.
- Animations respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; touch targets ≥ 44×44 px;
  number transitions animate (~400 ms ease-out), never snap.

