## Open Risks & Migration Plan

### Risks

- **R1 — P1 series bucket contract is unknown (blocking).** No document defines
  the field names inside P1 `/v1/series` buckets; `project_idea.md` explicitly
  says "assume similar structure to Sungrow" — and acting on that assumption
  shipped a bug: `legacy/src/p1-card.js` reads `energy_import_kwh` /
  `avg_power_w` from buckets where they don't exist, rendering NaN bars. **The
  contract must be captured from the live API and recorded in this document
  before any P1-series feature (Grid detail Day/Month/Year tabs) is built**
  (HC-006).
- **R2 — Lovable output unverified in detail.** Stack and file list are
  confirmed; component filenames, the chart library, and presence of TanStack
  Query/zod are expected-but-unconfirmed. Every "TBC" in this document resolves
  at M1; discrepancies amend this file, not silently the code.
- **R3 — Base-URL validation is prefix-only today.** The live deployment carries
  the vulnerability described in ADR-009 until the allowlist port lands (M4).
- **R4 — Bundle budget uncalibrated.** HC-005 numbers are provisional until the
  first real `vite build` (M3). If the delivered chart library blows the budget,
  ADR-007 amendment decides the replacement.
- **R5 — CSP `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` retained.** Inline style attributes
  from React/charts require it initially; audit and tighten (`style-src-attr`)
  post-migration.
- **R6 — Flutter bridge integration must be re-verified end-to-end.** The
  bootstrap handshake, `'null'`-origin acceptance, and `dashboardReady` dispatch
  are re-implemented in React; test in a real WebView before cutover, including
  visibility-gated polling behavior when the app backgrounds.
- **R7 — Legacy `computeFlows` reads dead `export_power_w`** (solar→grid never
  renders). Fixed at port time with a pinning test (Data Flow §3, Testing §1) —
  do not port the defect.
- **R8 — Deploy provenance mismatch** between ghcr image pull and on-VPS build
  paths (Build & Deployment); Operator contract requires one provable path.

